inithooks (2.3.6+keel3) trixie; urgency=low

  * run: export INITHOOKS_CONF whether or not the file exists. It was
    exported only inside the test that sources it, so a hook whose job is to
    create the file got an empty path: 29preseed of the headless and qemu
    overlays failed with an ambiguous redirect on every headless first boot,
    and no hook that ran after the file was created could read it by name.
  * tests: test-run.bats, the contract between the runner and a hook,
    including the real 29preseed of the buildtasks overlay.

 -- Marcos Mendez <mendez.foto@gmail.com>  Sat, 26 Sep 2026 20:57:50 +0000

inithooks (2.3.6+keel2) trixie; urgency=low

  * 00declarative: read /etc/keel/instance.yaml, and /etc/inithooks.yaml when
    that one is absent, instead of the second path only. The first appliance
    boot wrote the description to the first path and the hook read the
    second, so the description was ignored and the instance came up from an
    empty conf.
  * declarative.py: add --which, which prints the description that would be
    read, and name an ignored candidate in a warning when both exist.
  * default/inithooks: leave INITHOOKS_DECL unset by default, so the search
    happens; setting it still names a file outright.

 -- Marcos Mendez <mendez.foto@gmail.com>  Sat, 26 Sep 2026 20:11:13 +0000

inithooks (2.3.6+keel1) trixie; urgency=low

  * 01ipconfig: append the static options instead of overwriting the file.
  * 01ipconfig: keep the confconsole header and the IPv6 stanza when rewriting.
  * 01ipconfig: add the IP6_CONFIG, IP6_ADDRESS, IP6_GW, IP6_DNS1 and IP6_DNS2
    preseed keys.
  * 29tagid: only reload turnkey-init-fence when it is running.
  * turnkey-init-fence: skip the REDIRECT rule when the nat table is unavailable.
  * Add the firstboot hook 00declarative: renders /etc/inithooks.conf from
    /etc/inithooks.yaml before any other hook, with bin/declarative.py
    (--check, --render, --apply) as the reader; depend on python3-yaml.
  * Add lib/ipconfig.sh, lib/tagid.sh and lib/init-fence.sh, the shell
    functions of the hooks, installed under /usr/lib/inithooks/lib.
  * Add the tests: bats for the shell hooks, pytest for the declarative
    reader, with coverage checked on every pull request.

 -- Keel Linux maintainers <admin@keellinux.org>  Sat, 26 Sep 2026 14:58:05 +0000

